\ A 240 x 240 ST7789 on SPI1: PA5 SCL, PA7 SDA, PA4 CS, PB0 DC, PB1 RES.  ok.
\ Pixels while asleep, a command too soon after a reset, the colour mode  ok.
\ after reset, then a proper start, colours, and rows the panel hides.  ok.
#!attach 1 tft PA4 PA5 PA7 PB0 PB1
$48000000 constant GPIOA  $48000400 constant GPIOB  $40013000 constant SPI1  ok.
: ms ( n -- ) 15999 $E000E014 !  0 $E000E018 !  5 $E000E010 !  ok.
  0 ?do begin $E000E010 @ $10000 and until loop  0 $E000E010 ! ;  ok.
: pins ( -- )  ok.
  %11 $4002104C bis!  1 12 lshift $40021060 bis!  ok.
  1 4 lshift GPIOA $18 + !  %11 GPIOB $18 + !                     \ CS, DC, RES high  ok.
  $FF 8 lshift GPIOA bic!  %10001001 8 lshift GPIOA bis!          \ PA4 out, PA5 PA7 AF  ok.
  $F0F 20 lshift GPIOA $20 + bic!  $505 20 lshift GPIOA $20 + bis!  ok.
  $F GPIOB bic!  %0101 GPIOB bis!                                  \ PB0 PB1 out  ok.
  $1700 SPI1 4 + !  $34C SPI1 ! ;                                  \ master, 4 MHz  ok.
: idle ( -- ) begin SPI1 8 + @ $80 and 0= until ;                 \ BSY clear: the byte is out  ok.
: >spi ( b -- ) begin SPI1 8 + @ 2 and until  SPI1 $C + c! ;  ok.
: cs-lo 1 4 lshift 16 lshift GPIOA $18 + ! ;  : cs-hi idle 1 4 lshift GPIOA $18 + ! ;  ok.
: dc-cmd idle 1 16 lshift GPIOB $18 + ! ;  : dc-data idle 1 GPIOB $18 + ! ;  ok.
: cmd ( c -- ) cs-lo dc-cmd >spi cs-hi ;  ok.
: data ( b -- ) cs-lo dc-data >spi cs-hi ;  ok.
: 2data ( u -- ) dup 8 rshift data data ;  ok.
: window ( x0 y0 x1 y1 -- ) >r >r $2A cmd swap 2data r> 2data $2B cmd 2data r> 2data ;  ok.
0 variable colour  ok.
: fill ( x0 y0 x1 y1 c -- ) colour ! 2over 2over window  $2C cmd Redefine fill.  ok.
  cs-lo dc-data  rot - 1+ -rot swap - 1+ *  0 ?do colour @ dup 8 rshift >spi >spi loop  cs-hi ;  ok.
pins  ok.
0 0 7 7 $F800 fill  ok.

[chip] SPI1: overrun (OVR): a frame came in while the receive FIFO was full, and it is lost. Harmless when you only send; to read what comes back, read DR after every frame
[chip] ST7789: pixels in 18-bit colour, 3 bytes each (COLMOD 66, its value after reset). For RGB565, 2 bytes a pixel, send 3A 55 first
